/-!
# Cohen–Macaulay modules and schemes, field traces, cyclic covers

Let `(R, 𝔪)` be a local ring and `N` an `R`-module. The *dimension* of `N` is the Krull dimension
of its support. A sequence `x₁, …, x_r ∈ 𝔪` is `N`-*regular* if multiplication by `xᵢ` is
injective on `N/(x₁, …, x_{i-1})N` for every `i`, and the *depth* of `N` is the supremum of the
lengths of the `N`-regular sequences. `N` is *Cohen–Macaulay* if `N = 0` or `N` has a regular
sequence of length `dim N`. A sheaf of modules on a scheme is Cohen–Macaulay if all its stalks
are, and a scheme is Cohen–Macaulay if its structure sheaf is.

For a finite surjective morphism `f : Y ⟶ X` of varieties the *degree* of `f` is the degree of
the extension of function fields `K(Y)/K(X)` and `Tr_{Y/X} : K(Y) → K(X)` is its field trace.

Let `L` be a line bundle on a scheme `X`, `m > 0` and `s ∈ H⁰(X, Lᵐ)`. The *cyclic cover
algebra* is `𝒜(L, m, s) = Sym(L⁻¹)/I_s`, where `I_s` is generated by the local sections
`u - ⟨u, s⟩` for `u` a local section of `L⁻ᵐ = Symᵐ(L⁻¹)`, and the *cyclic cover* is
`p : Z = Spec_X 𝒜(L, m, s) ⟶ X`. It is *ramified* in general, along the zero scheme `(s = 0)`,
and *unramified* when `s = φ⁻¹(1)` for an isomorphism `φ : Lᵐ ≅ 𝒪_X`.

## Main definitions

* `MMP.Mori.IsRegularSequence`, `MMP.Mori.localDepth`: regular sequences in the maximal ideal and
  the depth of a module over a local ring; the dimension of a module is `Module.supportDim`.
* `MMP.Mori.IsCMModule`, `MMP.Mori.IsCMSheaf`, `MMP.Mori.IsCMAt`, `MMP.Mori.IsCMScheme`:
  Cohen–Macaulay modules, sheaves and schemes.
* `MMP.Mori.finiteDegree`, `MMP.Mori.fieldTrace`: the degree and the trace of a finite morphism
  of varieties on function fields.
* `MMP.Mori.symSpecFunction`, `MMP.Mori.cyclicCoverGenerator`: the functions on `Spec_X Sym(N)`
  given by sections of `Symᵏ(N)`, and the generators `u - ⟨u, s⟩`.
* `MMP.Mori.cyclicCoverIdeal`, `MMP.Mori.cyclicCover`, `MMP.Mori.cyclicCoverToBase`,
  `MMP.Mori.cyclicCoverAlgebra`, `MMP.Mori.cyclicCoverAlgebraIncl`: the ideal `I_s`, the cyclic
  cover `p : Z ⟶ X`, the algebra `𝒜(L, m, s)` and the maps `ιᵢ : L⁻ⁱ ⟶ 𝒜(L, m, s)`.
* `MMP.Mori.zeroSchemeIdeal`, `MMP.Mori.zeroScheme`: the zero scheme `(s = 0)` and its ideal.
* `MMP.Mori.ramifiedCyclicCover`, `MMP.Mori.unramifiedCyclicCover`: the two kinds of cyclic
  cover.

## Main results

* `MMP.Mori.ideal_cyclicCoverIdeal`: over an affine open of `Spec_X Sym(N)` lying over an affine
  open `W₀` of `X`, the ideal `I_s` is generated by the generators `u - ⟨u, s⟩` over `W₀`.
* `MMP.Mori.subschemeι_app_cyclicCoverGenerator`, `MMP.Mori.cyclicCoverAlgebraIncl_self`: the
  generators vanish on `Z`, that is `ιₘ(u) = p^*⟨u, s⟩`.
* `MMP.Mori.symSpecFunction_restrict`, `MMP.Mori.symSpecFunction_smul`,
  `MMP.Mori.cyclicCoverGenerator_restrict`, `MMP.Mori.cyclicCoverGenerator_smul`: the functions
  on `Spec_X Sym(N)` given by sections of `Symᵏ(N)`, and the generators `u - ⟨u, s⟩`, are
  compatible with restriction and `𝒪_X`-linear.

## Implementation notes

The source states the commutative-algebra definitions for finite modules over a local ring, for
coherent sheaves on a locally Noetherian scheme and for locally Noetherian schemes. Neither
finiteness nor the Noetherian hypotheses are needed to state them, so they are left to the
results. Likewise the degree and the trace are defined for every dominant morphism of integral
schemes, of which a finite surjective morphism of varieties is a case, and the cyclic covers over
every scheme, of which a normal variety is a case.

Regularity is `RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular`, the injectivity condition of the source,
and not `RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular`, which in addition requires `N/(x₁, …, x_r)N ≠ 0`: the
two agree for a nonzero finite module and a sequence in `𝔪`, by Nakayama's lemma, and the source
imposes only the injectivity.

The cyclic cover is written in terms of `N = L⁻¹` and of the pairing `σ = ⟨·, s⟩ : Symᵐ(N) ⟶ 𝒪_X`
rather than of `L` and `s`. For an invertible `N` the data `(N, σ)` and `(L, s)` determine each
other, since `Lᵐ = Hom(L⁻ᵐ, 𝒪_X)`, and in these terms the definition reads
`𝒜 = Sym(N)/(u - σ(u))`, the formula of the source. An isomorphism `φ : Lᵐ ≅ 𝒪_X` corresponds
to `σ = ⟨·, φ⁻¹(1)⟩` being an isomorphism.

The cover is built as the closed subscheme `Z` of `Spec_X Sym(N)` cut out by the ideal sheaf
generated by the sections `u - σ(u)`, and `𝒜(L, m, s)` is then `p_* 𝒪_Z`. Since
`Spec_X Sym(N) ⟶ X` is affine, `p_* 𝒪_Z = Sym(N)/I_s` and `Z = Spec_X (Sym(N)/I_s)`. The ideal
sheaf is given on each affine open `V` by the functions lying locally in the ideal generated by
the restrictions of the generators: over an affine open of `X` the generated quasi-coherent ideal
of the affine scheme `p⁻¹(W)` is the ideal generated by the `u - σ(u)`, and its sections on an
affine open contained in `p⁻¹(W)` are the extension of that ideal, so this family is exactly the
family of sections of the generated ideal sheaf, and `Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals` returns that
ideal sheaf. That the family is attained (`MMP.Mori.ideal_cyclicCoverIdeal`) is the
quasi-coherence of `Symᵐ(N)`: over a standard open `D(r)` of an affine `W₀` a section of `Symᵐ(N)`
is `x / rᵏ` with `x` a section over `W₀`, so the generators over any open become, near each point,
multiples of generators over `W₀` by units. In the same way the ideal of `(s = 0)` is the ideal
sheaf generated by the image of `σ`.

## References

* [J. Kollár, S. Mori, *Birational geometry of algebraic varieties*][KollarMori], 2.47, 2.49,
  2.50, 2.64, 5.1, 5.19
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite IsLocalRing

universe u

namespace MMP.Mori

/-! ### Regular sequences, depth and Cohen–Macaulay modules -/

section LocalRing

variable (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] (N : Type*) [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N]

/-- A sequence `x₁, …, x_r` of elements of the maximal ideal of a local ring `R` is
*`N`-regular* if, for every `i`, multiplication by `xᵢ` is injective on
`N/(x₁, …, x_{i-1})N`. -/
@[mmp "def_km5a_regular_sequence"]
def IsRegularSequence (xs : List R) : Prop :=
  (∀ x ∈ xs, x ∈ maximalIdeal R) ∧ RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular N xs

/-- The *depth* of a module `N` over a local ring `R`: the supremum, in `ℕ∞`, of the lengths of
the `N`-regular sequences in the maximal ideal. -/
@[mmp "def_km5a_depth"]
def localDepth : ℕ∞ :=
  ⨆ xs ∈ {xs : List R | IsRegularSequence R N xs}, (xs.length : ℕ∞)

/-- A module `N` over a local ring `R` is *Cohen–Macaulay* if `N = 0` or there is an
`N`-regular sequence in the maximal ideal whose length is the dimension `dim N` of `N`. -/
@[mmp "def_km5a_cm_module"]
def IsCMModule : Prop :=
  Subsingleton N ∨ ∃ xs : List R, IsRegularSequence R N xs ∧
    ((xs.length : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) = Module.supportDim R N

variable {R N}

/-- The length of a regular sequence is at most the depth. -/
theorem IsRegularSequence.length_le_localDepth {xs : List R} (h : IsRegularSequence R N xs) :
    (xs.length : ℕ∞) ≤ localDepth R N :=
  le_iSup₂_of_le (f := fun xs (_ : xs ∈ {xs : List R | IsRegularSequence R N xs}) =>
    (xs.length : ℕ∞)) xs h le_rfl

/-- The zero module is Cohen–Macaulay. -/
theorem isCMModule_of_subsingleton [Subsingleton N] : IsCMModule R N := Or.inl ‹_›

end LocalRing

/-! ### Cohen–Macaulay sheaves and schemes -/

section Scheme

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- A sheaf of `𝒪_X`-modules `F` is *Cohen–Macaulay* if for every point `x` the stalk `F_x` is a
Cohen–Macaulay module over the local ring `𝒪_{X,x}`. -/
@[mmp "def_km5a_cm_sheaf"]
def IsCMSheaf (F : X.Modules) : Prop :=
  ∀ x : X, IsCMModule (X.presheaf.stalk x) (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) F.val.presheaf x)

variable (X) in
/-- A scheme `X` is *Cohen–Macaulay at the point `x`* if the local ring `𝒪_{X,x}` is
Cohen–Macaulay as a module over itself. -/
@[mmp "def_km5a_cm_scheme"]
def IsCMAt (x : X) : Prop :=
  IsCMModule (X.presheaf.stalk x) (X.presheaf.stalk x)

variable (X) in
/-- A scheme `X` is *Cohen–Macaulay* if its structure sheaf `𝒪_X` is a Cohen–Macaulay sheaf of
`𝒪_X`-modules. -/
@[mmp "def_km5a_cm_scheme"]
def IsCMScheme : Prop :=
  IsCMSheaf (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf)

end Scheme

/-! ### Degree and trace of a finite morphism -/

section Trace

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : Y ⟶ X) [IsIntegral X] [IsIntegral Y] [IsDominant f]

/-- The *degree* `deg f = [K(Y) : K(X)]` of a dominant morphism `f : Y ⟶ X` of integral
schemes, the degree of the extension of function fields given by `f^*` (it is `0` if `K(Y)/K(X)`
is not finite). For a finite surjective morphism of varieties this is the degree of the finite
extension `K(Y)/K(X)`. -/
@[mmp "def_km2c_field_trace"]
def finiteDegree : ℕ :=
  letI := functionFieldMapAlgebra f
  Module.finrank X.functionField Y.functionField

/-- The *trace* `Tr_{Y/X} : K(Y) → K(X)` of a dominant morphism `f : Y ⟶ X` of integral schemes:
the field trace of the extension `K(Y)/K(X)` given by `f^*` (the zero map if `K(Y)/K(X)` is not
finite). For a finite surjective morphism of varieties the extension is finite and this is the
usual field trace. -/
@[mmp "def_km2c_field_trace"]
def fieldTrace : Y.functionField → X.functionField :=
  letI := functionFieldMapAlgebra f
  Algebra.trace X.functionField Y.functionField

end Trace

/-! ### Restriction of sections -/

section Restriction

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- Restricting a section in two steps is restricting it along the composite inclusion. -/
private lemma map_map_homOfLE {Y : Scheme.{u}} {U V W : Y.Opens} (h₁ : V ≤ U) (h₂ : W ≤ V)
    (a : Γ(Y, U)) :
    Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE h₂).op (Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE h₁).op a) =
      Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE (h₂.trans h₁)).op a := by
  rw [← CommRingCat.comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp]
  rfl

/-- Membership in an ideal of the sections over an affine open is local: it suffices that
around every point some standard open `D(g)` carries the section into the extended ideal. -/
private lemma mem_of_forall_exists_basicOpen {Y : Scheme.{u}} {V : Y.Opens} (hV : IsAffineOpen V)
    (I : Ideal Γ(Y, V)) (f : Γ(Y, V))
    (H : ∀ y ∈ V, ∃ g : Γ(Y, V), y ∈ Y.basicOpen g ∧
      Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE (Y.basicOpen_le g)).op f ∈
        I.map (Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE (Y.basicOpen_le g)).op).hom) : f ∈ I := by
  refine Submodule.mem_of_span_eq_top_of_smul_pow_mem I {g | ∃ n : ℕ, g ^ n * f ∈ I} ?_ f
    fun g => g.2
  rw [← hV.self_le_iSup_basicOpen_iff]
  intro y hy
  obtain ⟨g, hyg, hg⟩ := H y hy
  refine TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨g, ?_⟩, hyg⟩
  letI := (Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE (Y.basicOpen_le g)).op).hom.toAlgebra
  haveI := hV.isLocalization_basicOpen g
  obtain ⟨⟨a, c⟩, hac⟩ :=
    (IsLocalization.mem_map_algebraMap_iff (Submonoid.powers g) Γ(Y, Y.basicOpen g)).mp hg
  obtain ⟨⟨_, j, rfl⟩, hj⟩ := IsLocalization.exists_of_eq (M := Submonoid.powers g)
    (S := Γ(Y, Y.basicOpen g)) (x := f * c) (y := a) (by rw [map_mul]; exact hac)
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := c.2
  refine ⟨j + n, ?_⟩
  have e : g ^ (j + n) * f = g ^ j * a := by
    rw [← hj, ← hn]
    ring
  rw [e]
  exact I.mul_mem_left _ a.2

/-- A section of a quasi-coherent module over a standard open `D(r)` of an affine open `W₀`
becomes, after multiplication by a power of `r`, the restriction of a section over `W₀`. -/
private lemma exists_map_eq_pow_smul (M : X.Modules) [M.IsQuasicoherent] (W₀ : X.affineOpens)
    (r : Γ(X, W₀.1)) (u : Γ(M, X.basicOpen r)) :
    ∃ (x : Γ(M, W₀.1)) (k : ℕ), M.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le r)).op x =
      (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le r)).op r) ^ k • u := by
  letI := Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange.moduleOfLE M (X.basicOpen_le r)
  haveI := Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange.isLocalizedModule_restrictₗ
    M W₀.2 r rfl (X.basicOpen_le r)
  obtain ⟨⟨x, ⟨_, k, rfl⟩⟩, hx⟩ := IsLocalizedModule.surj (Submonoid.powers r)
    (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange.restrictₗ M (X.basicOpen_le r)) u
  refine ⟨x, k, ?_⟩
  rw [← map_pow]
  exact hx.symm

end Restriction

/-! ### Cyclic covers attached to a line bundle -/

section CyclicCover

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (N : X.Modules)
  [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N]

/-- The line bundle `N` on `X`, as the datum from which the symmetric algebra `Sym(N)` and the
total space `Spec_X Sym(N)` are built. -/
abbrev cyclicCoverSituation : Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.{u} := ⟨X, X, 𝟙 X, N⟩

/-- The relative spectrum `Spec_X Sym(N)` of the symmetric algebra of `N`. -/
abbrev symSpec : Scheme.{u} := (cyclicCoverSituation N).totalSpace

/-- The structure morphism `Spec_X Sym(N) ⟶ X`. -/
abbrev symSpecToBase : symSpec N ⟶ X := (cyclicCoverSituation N).totalSpaceToBase

/-- A local section `x` of `Symᵏ(N)` over an open `W ⊆ X`, viewed as a function on the preimage
of `W` in `Spec_X Sym(N)`, through `Symᵏ(N) ⊆ Sym(N)`. -/
def symSpecFunction (k : ℕ) (W : X.Opens)
    (x : ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (k : ℤ)).val.obj (op W)) :
    Γ(symSpec N, symSpecToBase N ⁻¹ᵁ W) :=
  ((Stacks.RelativeSpec.universalAlgebraMap
      (cyclicCoverSituation N).relativeSpecSituation).right.app (op W)).hom
    ((cyclicCoverSituation N).algebraSheafIncl k W x)

/-- The inclusion of a homogeneous section into the algebra sheaf commutes with restriction. -/
private lemma algebraSheafIncl_restrict (k : ℤ) {W W' : X.Opens} (h : W' ≤ W)
    (x : ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece k).val.obj (op W)) :
    ((cyclicCoverSituation N).algebraSheaf.right.obj.map (homOfLE h).op).hom
        ((cyclicCoverSituation N).algebraSheafIncl k W x) =
      (cyclicCoverSituation N).algebraSheafIncl k W'
        (((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece k).val.map (homOfLE h).op x) :=
  (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
    (((sheafificationAdjunction (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : TopCat))
      CommRingCat.{u}).unit.app (Stacks.RelativeSpec.ungradedCommPresheaf X
        (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra
        (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra_mul_comm)).naturality
        (homOfLE h).op) _).symm.trans
      (congrArg (Stacks.RelativeSpec.ungradedCommUnit X (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra
        (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra_mul_comm W').hom
        ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.totalRestrict_incl
          (homOfLE h).op k x))

/-- Restricting `symSpecFunction N k W x` to the preimage of `W' ⊆ W` gives the function attached
to the restriction of `x` to `W'`. -/
theorem symSpecFunction_restrict (k : ℕ) {W W' : X.Opens} (h : W' ≤ W)
    (x : ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (k : ℤ)).val.obj (op W)) :
    (symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE ((symSpecToBase N).preimage_mono h)).op
        (symSpecFunction N k W x) =
      symSpecFunction N k W'
        (((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (k : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE h).op x) := by
  have := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom ((Stacks.RelativeSpec.universalAlgebraMap
      (cyclicCoverSituation N).relativeSpecSituation).right.naturality (homOfLE h).op)
    ((cyclicCoverSituation N).algebraSheafIncl k W x)
  unfold symSpecFunction
  exact this.symm.trans (congrArg _ (algebraSheafIncl_restrict N k h x))

/-- `symSpecFunction` is linear over `𝒪_X`: the function attached to `a • x` is the pullback of `a`
times the function attached to `x`. -/
theorem symSpecFunction_smul (k : ℕ) (W : X.Opens) (a : X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W))
    (x : ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (k : ℤ)).val.obj (op W)) :
    symSpecFunction N k W (a • x) = (symSpecToBase N).app W a * symSpecFunction N k W x := by
  unfold symSpecFunction
  rw [Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.algebraSheafIncl_smul]
  refine (map_mul _ _ _).trans (congrArg (· * _) ?_)
  exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (NatTrans.congr_app (Under.w
    (Stacks.RelativeSpec.universalAlgebraMap
      (cyclicCoverSituation N).relativeSpecSituation)) (op W)) a

variable (m : ℕ)
  (σ : (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ⟶
    SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf)

/-- The generator `u - ⟨u, s⟩` of the ideal `I_s`, for a local section `u` of `Symᵐ(N)` over an
open `W ⊆ X`, as a function on the preimage of `W` in `Spec_X Sym(N)`; here `σ = ⟨·, s⟩`. -/
def cyclicCoverGenerator (W : X.Opens)
    (u : ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W)) :
    Γ(symSpec N, symSpecToBase N ⁻¹ᵁ W) :=
  symSpecFunction N m W u - (symSpecToBase N).app W (σ.val.app (op W) u)

/-- The generators `u - ⟨u, s⟩` are compatible with restriction. -/
theorem cyclicCoverGenerator_restrict {W W' : X.Opens} (h : W' ≤ W)
    (u : ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W)) :
    (symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE ((symSpecToBase N).preimage_mono h)).op
        (cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ W u) =
      cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ W'
        (((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE h).op u) := by
  unfold cyclicCoverGenerator
  rw [map_sub, symSpecFunction_restrict N m h]
  congr 1
  have h₁ := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (σ.val.naturality (homOfLE h).op) u
  have h₂ := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom ((symSpecToBase N).naturality (homOfLE h).op)
    (σ.val.app (op W) u)
  exact h₂.symm.trans (congrArg _ h₁.symm)

/-- The generator of a multiple `a • u` is the multiple of the generator by the pullback of `a`. -/
theorem cyclicCoverGenerator_smul (W : X.Opens) (a : X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W))
    (u : ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W)) :
    cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ W (a • u) =
      (symSpecToBase N).app W a * cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ W u := by
  unfold cyclicCoverGenerator
  rw [symSpecFunction_smul, map_smul, mul_sub]
  congr 1
  exact map_mul ((symSpecToBase N).app W).hom a _

/-- A function `f` on an open `V` of `Spec_X Sym(N)` lies *locally in `I_s`* if every point of
`V` has an affine open neighbourhood `V' ⊆ V`, lying over an open `W ⊆ X`, on which `f` is a
combination of the generators `u - ⟨u, s⟩` with `u` a section of `Symᵐ(N)` over `W`. -/
def IsLocallyInCyclicCoverIdeal (V : (symSpec N).Opens) (f : Γ(symSpec N, V)) : Prop :=
  ∀ y ∈ V, ∃ (W : X.Opens) (V' : (symSpec N).affineOpens) (h₁ : V'.1 ≤ V)
    (h₂ : V'.1 ≤ symSpecToBase N ⁻¹ᵁ W), y ∈ V'.1 ∧
    (symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE h₁).op f ∈
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun u =>
        (symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE h₂).op (cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ W u))

/-- The ideal sheaf on `Spec_X Sym(N)` generated by the local sections `u - ⟨u, s⟩`, `u` a local
section of `Symᵐ(N)`: on an affine open it consists of the functions lying locally in the ideal
generated by these sections, and over an affine open lying over an affine open `W₀` of `X` this
is the ideal generated by the sections over `W₀` (`ideal_cyclicCoverIdeal`). Its push-forward to
`X` is the ideal `I_s ⊆ Sym(N)`. -/
def cyclicCoverIdeal : (symSpec N).IdealSheafData :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals fun V =>
    Ideal.span {f | IsLocallyInCyclicCoverIdeal N m σ V.1 f}

/-- The ideal generated by the restrictions of the generators over `W` to an open `V`. -/
private lemma map_span_range_cyclicCoverGenerator {W : X.Opens} {V V' : (symSpec N).Opens}
    (h : V ≤ symSpecToBase N ⁻¹ᵁ W) (h' : V' ≤ V) :
    (Ideal.span (Set.range fun u => (symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op
        (cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ W u))).map ((symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE h').op).hom =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun u => (symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE (h'.trans h)).op
        (cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ W u)) := by
  rw [Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
  exact congrArg (fun F => Ideal.span (Set.range F)) (funext fun u => map_map_homOfLE h h' _)

/-- **Quasi-coherence of `Symᵐ(N)` for the generators.** On an affine open `V` lying over an
affine open `W₀` and over an open `W`, the restriction of a generator over `W` lies in the ideal
generated by the restrictions of the generators over `W₀`. -/
theorem map_cyclicCoverGenerator_mem_span (W₀ : X.affineOpens) {W : X.Opens}
    (V : (symSpec N).affineOpens) (h₀ : V.1 ≤ symSpecToBase N ⁻¹ᵁ W₀.1)
    (h : V.1 ≤ symSpecToBase N ⁻¹ᵁ W)
    (u : ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W)) :
    (symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op (cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ W u) ∈
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun x => (symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE h₀).op
        (cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ W₀.1 x)) := by
  refine mem_of_forall_exists_basicOpen V.2 _ _ fun y hy => ?_
  obtain ⟨r, hrW, hyr⟩ := W₀.2.exists_basicOpen_le ⟨_, h hy⟩ (h₀ hy)
  have hrW₀ := X.basicOpen_le r
  haveI := (cyclicCoverSituation N).isQuasicoherent_symmetricAlgebra_piece m
  obtain ⟨x, k, hx'⟩ := exists_map_eq_pow_smul
    ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ)) W₀ r
    (((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE hrW).op u)
  set g := (symSpecToBase N).appLE W₀.1 V.1 h₀ r with hg
  have hDg : (symSpec N).basicOpen g ≤ symSpecToBase N ⁻¹ᵁ X.basicOpen r := by
    rw [hg, Scheme.basicOpen_appLE]
    exact inf_le_right
  refine ⟨g, by rw [hg, Scheme.basicOpen_appLE]; exact ⟨hy, hyr⟩, ?_⟩
  have hu : IsUnit ((symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE ((symSpec N).basicOpen_le g)).op g) :=
    (symSpec N).toRingedSpace.isUnit_res_basicOpen g
  have hg' : (symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE ((symSpec N).basicOpen_le g)).op g =
      (symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE hDg).op ((symSpecToBase N).app (X.basicOpen r)
        (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hrW₀).op r)) := by
    simp only [hg, ← CommRingCat.comp_apply, Scheme.Hom.app_eq_appLE, Scheme.Hom.appLE_map,
      Scheme.Hom.map_appLE]
  have e₁ : (symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE ((symSpec N).basicOpen_le g)).op
      ((symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op (cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ W u)) =
      (symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE hDg).op
        (cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ _
          (((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.map
            (homOfLE hrW).op u)) := by
    rw [map_map_homOfLE, ← cyclicCoverGenerator_restrict N m σ hrW, map_map_homOfLE]
  have e₂ : (symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE ((symSpec N).basicOpen_le g)).op
      ((symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE h₀).op (cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ W₀.1 x)) =
      (symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE hDg).op
        (cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ _
          (((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.map
            (homOfLE hrW₀).op x)) := by
    erw [map_map_homOfLE, ← cyclicCoverGenerator_restrict N m σ hrW₀, map_map_homOfLE]
  refine (Ideal.mul_unit_mem_iff_mem _ (hu.pow k)).mp ?_
  rw [mul_comm, hg', ← map_pow, e₁, ← map_mul, ← map_pow]
  erw [← cyclicCoverGenerator_smul]
  erw [← hx', ← e₂]
  exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ (Ideal.subset_span ⟨x, rfl⟩)

/-- On an affine open `V` lying over an affine open `W₀`, a function lies locally in `I_s` exactly
when it lies in the ideal generated by the restrictions of the generators over `W₀`. -/
theorem span_isLocallyInCyclicCoverIdeal_eq (W₀ : X.affineOpens) (V : (symSpec N).affineOpens)
    (h₀ : V.1 ≤ symSpecToBase N ⁻¹ᵁ W₀.1) :
    Ideal.span {f | IsLocallyInCyclicCoverIdeal N m σ V.1 f} =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun x => (symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE h₀).op
        (cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ W₀.1 x)) := by
  apply le_antisymm
  · rw [Ideal.span_le]
    intro f hf
    refine mem_of_forall_exists_basicOpen V.2 _ _ fun y hy => ?_
    obtain ⟨W, V', h₁, h₂, hyV', hV'⟩ := hf y hy
    obtain ⟨g, hgV', hyg⟩ := V.2.exists_basicOpen_le ⟨y, hyV'⟩ hy
    refine ⟨g, hyg, ?_⟩
    rw [map_span_range_cyclicCoverGenerator, ← map_map_homOfLE h₁ hgV']
    have := Ideal.mem_map_of_mem ((symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE hgV').op).hom hV'
    rw [map_span_range_cyclicCoverGenerator] at this
    refine (Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_) this
    rintro _ ⟨x, rfl⟩
    exact map_cyclicCoverGenerator_mem_span N m σ W₀ ⟨_, V.2.basicOpen g⟩ _ _ x
  · rw [Ideal.span_le]
    rintro _ ⟨x, rfl⟩
    refine Ideal.subset_span fun y hy => ⟨W₀.1, V, le_rfl, h₀, hy, ?_⟩
    rw [map_map_homOfLE]
    exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨x, rfl⟩

/-- The ideal sheaf glued from the ideals `span (u - ⟨u, s⟩)` on the affine opens lying over an
affine open of `X`. -/
private def cyclicCoverIdealData : (symSpec N).IdealSheafData :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofAffineFamily
    (fun V => ∃ W₀ : X.affineOpens, V.1 ≤ symSpecToBase N ⁻¹ᵁ W₀.1)
    (fun V => Ideal.span {f | IsLocallyInCyclicCoverIdeal N m σ V.1 f})
    (fun y => by
      obtain ⟨W₀, hW₀, hy, -⟩ := Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp (X.isBasis_affineOpens)
        (show symSpecToBase N y ∈ (⊤ : X.Opens) from trivial)
      obtain ⟨V, hV, hyV, hVW⟩ := Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp ((symSpec N).isBasis_affineOpens)
        (show y ∈ symSpecToBase N ⁻¹ᵁ W₀ from hy)
      exact ⟨⟨V, hV⟩, ⟨⟨W₀, hW₀⟩, hVW⟩, hyV⟩)
    (fun U f ⟨W₀, h⟩ => ⟨W₀, ((symSpec N).basicOpen_le f).trans h⟩)
    (fun U V h ⟨W₀, hU⟩ _ => by
      rw [span_isLocallyInCyclicCoverIdeal_eq N m σ W₀ U hU,
        span_isLocallyInCyclicCoverIdeal_eq N m σ W₀ V ((show V.1 ≤ U.1 from h).trans hU)]
      exact map_span_range_cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ hU h)

private lemma cyclicCoverIdealData_le : cyclicCoverIdealData N m σ ≤ cyclicCoverIdeal N m σ := by
  refine Scheme.IdealSheafData.le_ofIdeals_iff.mpr fun V f hf => Ideal.subset_span fun y hy => ?_
  obtain ⟨W₀, hW₀, hyW₀, -⟩ := Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp (X.isBasis_affineOpens)
    (show symSpecToBase N y ∈ (⊤ : X.Opens) from trivial)
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hyg⟩ :=
    V.2.exists_basicOpen_le ⟨y, (show y ∈ symSpecToBase N ⁻¹ᵁ W₀ from hyW₀)⟩ hy
  have := (Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_ofAffineFamilyIdeal _ _).mp hf ⟨_, V.2.basicOpen g⟩
    ⟨⟨W₀, hW₀⟩, hg⟩ ((symSpec N).basicOpen_le g)
  rw [span_isLocallyInCyclicCoverIdeal_eq N m σ ⟨W₀, hW₀⟩ ⟨_, V.2.basicOpen g⟩ hg] at this
  exact ⟨W₀, ⟨_, V.2.basicOpen g⟩, (symSpec N).basicOpen_le g, hg, hyg, this⟩

/-- **The sections of `I_s` over an affine open.** Over an affine open `V` of `Spec_X Sym(N)`
lying over an affine open `W₀` of `X`, the ideal `I_s` is generated by the restrictions of the
generators `u - ⟨u, s⟩`, `u` a section of `Symᵐ(N)` over `W₀`. -/
theorem ideal_cyclicCoverIdeal (W₀ : X.affineOpens) (V : (symSpec N).affineOpens)
    (h₀ : V.1 ≤ symSpecToBase N ⁻¹ᵁ W₀.1) :
    (cyclicCoverIdeal N m σ).ideal V =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun x => (symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE h₀).op
        (cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ W₀.1 x)) := by
  rw [← span_isLocallyInCyclicCoverIdeal_eq N m σ W₀ V h₀]
  refine le_antisymm (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_ofIdeals_le _ _) ?_
  exact (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_ofAffineFamily _ _ _ _ _ ⟨W₀, h₀⟩).symm.le.trans
    (cyclicCoverIdealData_le N m σ V)

/-- The restriction of a generator `u - ⟨u, s⟩` to an affine open lies in `I_s`. -/
theorem map_cyclicCoverGenerator_mem_ideal {W : X.Opens} (V : (symSpec N).affineOpens)
    (h : V.1 ≤ symSpecToBase N ⁻¹ᵁ W)
    (u : ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W)) :
    (symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op (cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ W u) ∈
      (cyclicCoverIdeal N m σ).ideal V := by
  refine cyclicCoverIdealData_le N m σ V
    ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_ofAffineFamilyIdeal _ _).mpr fun U _ hUV => ?_)
  refine (congrArg (· ∈ _) (map_map_homOfLE h hUV _)).mpr
    (Ideal.subset_span fun y hy => ⟨W, U, le_rfl, (show U.1 ≤ V.1 from hUV).trans h, hy, ?_⟩)
  exact (congrArg (· ∈ _) (map_map_homOfLE _ _ _)).mpr (Ideal.subset_span ⟨u, rfl⟩)

/-- The *cyclic cover* `Z = Spec_X 𝒜(L, m, s)`, where `𝒜(L, m, s) = Sym(L⁻¹)/I_s`: the closed
subscheme of `Spec_X Sym(N)` cut out by `I_s`, for `N = L⁻¹` and `σ = ⟨·, s⟩`. -/
abbrev cyclicCover : Scheme.{u} := (cyclicCoverIdeal N m σ).subscheme

/-- The structure morphism `p : Spec_X 𝒜(L, m, s) ⟶ X` of the cyclic cover. -/
def cyclicCoverToBase : cyclicCover N m σ ⟶ X :=
  (cyclicCoverIdeal N m σ).subschemeι ≫ symSpecToBase N

/-- The *cyclic cover algebra* `𝒜(L, m, s) = Sym(L⁻¹)/I_s`, the quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-algebra
`p_* 𝒪_Z` of the cyclic cover `p : Z ⟶ X`. -/
@[mmp "def_km2c_cyclic_cover_algebra"]
def cyclicCoverAlgebra : Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf X :=
  Stacks.AffineAlgebraEquivalence.pushforwardAlgebra (cyclicCoverToBase N m σ)

/-- The map `ιᵢ : L⁻ⁱ = Symⁱ(L⁻¹) ⟶ 𝒜(L, m, s)`, the inclusion into `Sym(L⁻¹)` followed by the
quotient map, on local sections over an open `W ⊆ X`. -/
@[mmp "def_km2c_cyclic_cover_algebra"]
def cyclicCoverAlgebraIncl (i : ℕ) (W : X.Opens)
    (x : ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (i : ℤ)).val.obj (op W)) :
    Γ(cyclicCover N m σ, cyclicCoverToBase N m σ ⁻¹ᵁ W) :=
  (cyclicCoverIdeal N m σ).subschemeι.app (symSpecToBase N ⁻¹ᵁ W) (symSpecFunction N i W x)

/-- **The generators vanish on the cyclic cover**: `u - ⟨u, s⟩` restricts to zero on `Z`. -/
theorem subschemeι_app_cyclicCoverGenerator (W : X.Opens)
    (u : ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W)) :
    (cyclicCoverIdeal N m σ).subschemeι.app (symSpecToBase N ⁻¹ᵁ W)
      (cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ W u) = 0 := by
  have hV : ∀ z : ((cyclicCoverIdeal N m σ).subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ (symSpecToBase N ⁻¹ᵁ W) : Set _),
      ∃ V : (symSpec N).affineOpens, (cyclicCoverIdeal N m σ).subschemeι z.1 ∈ V.1 ∧
        V.1 ≤ symSpecToBase N ⁻¹ᵁ W := fun z => by
    obtain ⟨V, hV, hzV, hVW⟩ := Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp ((symSpec N).isBasis_affineOpens)
      (show (cyclicCoverIdeal N m σ).subschemeι z.1 ∈ symSpecToBase N ⁻¹ᵁ W from z.2)
    exact ⟨⟨V, hV⟩, hzV, hVW⟩
  choose V hzV hVW using hV
  refine TopCat.Sheaf.eq_of_locally_eq' (cyclicCover N m σ).sheaf
    (fun z => (cyclicCoverIdeal N m σ).subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ (V z).1) _
    (fun z => homOfLE ((cyclicCoverIdeal N m σ).subschemeι.preimage_mono (hVW z)))
    (fun z hz => Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨z, hz⟩, hzV ⟨z, hz⟩⟩) _ _ fun z => ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (map_zero _).symm
  have e := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
    ((cyclicCoverIdeal N m σ).subschemeι.naturality (homOfLE (hVW z)).op)
    (cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ W u)
  refine e.symm.trans ?_
  change ((cyclicCoverIdeal N m σ).subschemeι.app (V z).1).hom
    (((symSpec N).presheaf.map (homOfLE (hVW z)).op).hom (cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ W u)) = 0
  rw [← RingHom.mem_ker, Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_subschemeι_app]
  exact map_cyclicCoverGenerator_mem_ideal N m σ (V z) (hVW z) u

/-- **The defining relation of the cyclic cover algebra**: `ιₘ(u) = p^*⟨u, s⟩` for a local
section `u` of `L⁻ᵐ`. -/
theorem cyclicCoverAlgebraIncl_self (W : X.Opens)
    (u : ((cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ)).val.obj (op W)) :
    cyclicCoverAlgebraIncl N m σ m W u =
      (cyclicCoverToBase N m σ).app W (σ.val.app (op W) u) := by
  have h := subschemeι_app_cyclicCoverGenerator N m σ W u
  unfold cyclicCoverGenerator at h
  rw [map_sub, sub_eq_zero] at h
  unfold cyclicCoverAlgebraIncl cyclicCoverToBase
  rw [h, Scheme.Hom.comp_app]
  rfl

/-- The ideal sheaf on `X` of the zero scheme `(s = 0)`: the ideal sheaf generated by the image
of `⟨·, s⟩ : L⁻ᵐ ⟶ 𝒪_X`. -/
def zeroSchemeIdeal : X.IdealSheafData :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals fun V => Ideal.span (Set.range (σ.val.app (op V.1)))

/-- The *zero scheme* `(s = 0)`: the closed subscheme of `X` whose ideal is the image of
`⟨·, s⟩ : L⁻ᵐ ⟶ 𝒪_X`. -/
@[mmp "def_km2c_cyclic_cover_algebra"]
abbrev zeroScheme : Scheme.{u} := (zeroSchemeIdeal N m σ).subscheme

/-- The *ramified cyclic cover* `p : Z = Spec_X 𝒜(L, m, s) ⟶ X` attached to a line bundle `L`,
`m > 0` and `s ∈ H⁰(X, Lᵐ)`, here written through `N = L⁻¹` and `σ = ⟨·, s⟩`. -/
@[mmp "def_km2c_ramified_cyclic_cover"]
abbrev ramifiedCyclicCover : cyclicCover N m σ ⟶ X := cyclicCoverToBase N m σ

/-- The *unramified cyclic cover* `p : X_{m,L} = Spec_X 𝒜(L, m, s_φ) ⟶ X` attached to an
isomorphism `φ : Lᵐ ≅ 𝒪_X`, with `s_φ = φ⁻¹(1)`: written through `N = L⁻¹`, the pairing
`⟨·, s_φ⟩ : L⁻ᵐ ⟶ 𝒪_X` is the isomorphism `ψ`. -/
@[mmp "def_km2c_unramified_cyclic_cover"]
abbrev unramifiedCyclicCover (ψ : (cyclicCoverSituation N).symmetricAlgebra.piece (m : ℤ) ≅
    SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf) : cyclicCover N m ψ.hom ⟶ X :=
  cyclicCoverToBase N m ψ.hom

end CyclicCover

end MMP.Mori

end
